      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The case of a 33-year-old woman suffering from a paradoxical peripheral embolism in the presence of a right-to-left shunt at the level of an ostium secundum defect is presented. A functional stenosis of the tricuspid valve due to obstruction through a thrombotic atrial mass was found to be responsible for the right-to-left shunt. Treatment consisted of peripheral embolectomy, removal of the atrial mass, and closure of the atrial septum defect."},
